{
  "comment": "One row per asset Blender makes (#801 to #808). `npm run blender:render <pack>` runs tools/blender/packs/<script> once per row, on one of Devon's machines with Blender 5.2, and writes assets/blender/<pack>/<name>.glb and its tools/blender/manifest.json row. Every key of a row is in its source hash, so editing a row without a render is check 8 line 4. `packs.<pack>.extraColours` is at most 8 colours outside tools/pixel/textures.json's palettes, each with a `why`.",
  "packs": {
    "calibration": {
      "extraColours": []
    },
    "evidence": {
      "extraColours": [
        {
          "colour": "#e6d9a8",
          "why": "Tallow. The candle-count quest and the chapel candle clue are tallow candles, and the castle's palettes stop at plaster #cbbfa3, which reads as stone beside a wall of it, not as a candle."
        }
      ]
    },
    "countryside": {
      "extraColours": [
        {
          "colour": "#b89d55",
          "why": "Wheat, and the rick. The castle's palettes have no yellow above plaster #cbbfa3 and wooden_gate's browns, so a field of standing corn at 60 m in the fog would read as bare earth or as stone."
        },
        {
          "colour": "#6b7a3a",
          "why": "Meadow. Every green in tools/pixel/textures.json is forest_ground_06 or grassy_cobblestone, moss and shade at most #5b6a36, and a hay meadow beside a ploughed strip needs one green lighter than the slopes behind it, or the fields are one colour under fog."
        },
        {
          "colour": "#7e6a3e",
          "why": "Thatch, for the longhouse and barn roofs. The castle roofs are slate and tile, and a farm under a slate roof reads as a second castle at 100 m."
        }
      ]
    },
    "folk": {
      "extraColours": [
        {
          "colour": "#d9aa84",
          "why": "Skin. The castle's palettes are stone, wood, plaster and moss, and the nearest thing to a face in them is wood_floor_deck #a17f58, which reads as a wooden mask. `Bare`, so the tint never touches it (#820)."
        },
        {
          "colour": "#d0b096",
          "why": "Skin, for the two old heads: paler and greyer than the first, so an old face differs from a young one by more than its brows at the distance a player passes one."
        },
        {
          "colour": "#ebe5d6",
          "why": "Undyed linen, the lightest `Cloth` swatch. The tint multiplies `Cloth`, so a garment can only be as light as its swatch, and the palettes stop at plaster #cbbfa3, which would darken every tint by a fifth (SPECS.md, \"Two materials over the one atlas image\"; #644, #684)."
        }
      ]
    },
    "held": {
      "extraColours": []
    }
  },
