      "seed": "folk/2026-10-03",
      "why": "The household's shared body (#820 to #823): one 20-joint rig, 22 parts in five slots a person picks from by `parts`, and eleven clips. `rig` is each joint's place in metres in the model frame (+x the body's left, +y up, +z the way it faces); every joint keeps the model's own axes, so a joint's rotation at rest is none. `parts` is the catalogue, one mesh node each, `Cloth` tinted and `Bare` not. `clips` is tools/bodies/clips.json's grammar over this rig's own Idle: the angle at key k of `keys` is rest + amp * sin(2 pi (cycles * k / keys + phase)), a rotation about a model axis at the joint, composed on Idle's at that key; `cycles` is an integer or the clip does not loop, and `driver` is the joint test/assets.mjs holds 20 degrees off Idle. `sheet` is the six people the contact sheet lines up. The first wearer is the hen-wife.",
